It is late in the evening in Berlin, but in Mexico it is now midday.
I put the mobile phone on the table for my video call.
My parents, my sister Sofia and my brother Diego are all on the screen.
Even our dog Lola is there!
They all sing loudly for me.
The song was a bit chaotic, but very beautiful.
"Thank you for the song!" I say happily.
"Do you all have the day off today?" I ask them.
My father laughs and says: "Yes, we are celebrating your birthday here!"
I ask my sister: "Sofia, how was your week at the university?"
"I had a lot of exams, but now I am on holiday," she answers.
Then I look at my brother.
"And Diego, didn't you have an important football match yesterday?"
He nods proudly and says: "Yes, the match was great and we won!"
Suddenly I see a shoe in the background.
"Is Lola actually still stealing shoes?" I ask laughing.
My mother sighs and turns the camera to the dog.
Lola has my father's old slipper in her mouth.
"She was good this morning, but now she is looking for toys again," my father jokes.
I miss my family, but I am really happy today.
